<div class="frr-wrap">
  <p class="frr-lead">
    <strong>FRRouting packages</strong> for this host — install/start daemons
    (<code>zebra</code>, OpenFabric <code>fabricd</code>, …).
    Not the stock <strong>Routing Table</strong> tab (kernel routes only).
  </p>

  <div class="frr-companion">
    <strong>When:</strong> rings / multi-hop / Proxmox+Unraid fabrics.
    <strong>Skip:</strong> single static TB cable only.
    <br>
<?php if ($tbn): ?>
    <strong>Thunderbolt Net:</strong> installed — OpenFabric <em>policy</em> on
    <a href="/Settings/NetworkSettings">Network Settings → Thunderbolt</a>
    (Advanced). This tab = packages only.
<?php else: ?>
    <strong>Thunderbolt Net:</strong> optional
    (<a href="https://github.com/ibigsnet/ThunderboltNet" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub</a>) for TB + OpenFabric policy.
<?php endif; ?>
    <span class="frr-muted"> · Not USB4STREAM / <code>thunderbolt_stream</code></span>
  </div>

  <div class="frr-section" style="margin-top:0.5em">
    <h3>Status</h3>
    <table class="frr-status tablesorter shift">
      <tr>
        <td>Plugin</td>
        <td><code><?= $ver ?></code>
          <span class="frr-muted"> — Plugins tab updates</span></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Unraid product</td>
        <td><code><?= $uver ?></code> · <code><?= $arch ?></code>
          <span class="frr-muted"> — picks package bundle (not kernel)</span></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>FRR live</td>
        <td>
<?php if ($frr_ok): ?>
          <span class="frr-badge frr-badge-ok">Present</span>
          <?php if (!empty($det['version'])): ?>
            <code class="frr-muted"><?= htmlspecialchars($det['version']) ?></code>
          <?php endif; ?>
<?php else: ?>
          <span class="frr-badge frr-badge-warn">Not installed</span>
          <span class="frr-muted"> — Apply to download when a bundle exists</span>
<?php endif; ?>
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Daemons</td>
        <td>
          <span class="frr-badge <?= $zebra_run ? 'frr-badge-ok' : 'frr-badge-bad' ?>"><?= $zebra_run ? 'zebra up' : 'zebra down' ?></span>
          <span class="frr-badge <?= $fabricd_run ? 'frr-badge-ok' : 'frr-badge-bad' ?>"><?= $fabricd_run ? 'fabricd up' : 'fabricd down' ?></span>
          <span class="frr-muted"> · <?= htmlspecialchars($det['note'] ?? '') ?></span>
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Catalog bundle</td>
        <td>
<?php if ($bundle_ok): ?>
          <span class="frr-badge frr-badge-ok">Match</span>
          FRR <code><?= htmlspecialchars($bundle['frr_version'] ?? '') ?></code>
          · channel <code><?= htmlspecialchars($bundle['channel'] ?? '') ?></code>
<?php else: ?>
          <span class="frr-badge frr-badge-warn">No match yet</span>
          <span class="frr-muted"><?= htmlspecialchars($bundle['error'] ?? 'resolving…') ?></span>
<?php endif; ?>
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Flash package cache</td>
        <td><?= $pk
          ? count($pk) . ' managed file(s)'
          : '<span class="frr-muted">Empty — Apply auto-downloads when available</span>' ?></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Thunderbolt Net</td>
        <td><?= $tbn
          ? '<span class="frr-ok">Installed</span> <span class="frr-muted">— policy on Thunderbolt tab</span>'
          : '<span class="frr-muted">Not installed (OK)</span>' ?></td>
      </tr>
    </table>
    <dl>
      <dt>Status fields:</dt>
      <dd class="frr-muted">Live FRR · catalog · companions</dd>
    </dl>
    <blockquote class="inline_help">
      Fully automated like the Nvidia Driver plugin: catalog → download → <code>installpkg</code> → enable daemons → start.
      Matched to <strong>Unraid product version + arch</strong>, not <code>uname -r</code>.
      Defaults do not put eth0/br0 into any protocol.
      <a href="https://github.com/ibigsnet/UnraidFRR/blob/main/docs/scope-and-safety.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Scope &amp; safety ↗</a>
      ·
      <a href="https://github.com/ibigsnet/UnraidFRR/blob/main/DOCS.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener">DOCS ↗</a>
    </blockquote>
  </div>

  <form method="POST" action="/update.php" target="progressFrame">
    <input type="hidden" name="#file" value="UnraidFRR/UnraidFRR.cfg">
    <input type="hidden" name="#include" value="/plugins/UnraidFRR/include/frr-update.php">

    <div class="frr-section">
      <h3>Packages</h3>
      <p class="frr-section-lead">How FRR is downloaded and rehydrated after reboot.</p>

      <dl>
        <dt>Package channel:</dt>
        <dd>
          <select name="package_channel">
            <?= mk_option($cfg['package_channel'] ?? 'latest', 'latest', 'Latest stable (recommended)') ?>
            <?= mk_option($cfg['package_channel'] ?? 'latest', 'previous', 'Previous stable (rollback)') ?>
          </select>
        </dd>
      </dl>
      <blockquote class="inline_help">
        Automated set from the project catalog. Channels appear as builds are published.
      </blockquote>

      <dl>
        <dt>Auto-download packages:</dt>
        <dd>
          <select name="auto_download">
            <?= mk_option($cfg['auto_download'] ?? 'yes', 'yes', 'Yes (default — fully automatic)') ?>
            <?= mk_option($cfg['auto_download'] ?? 'yes', 'no', 'No — use flash cache only') ?>
          </select>
        </dd>
      </dl>
      <blockquote class="inline_help">
        <strong>Yes:</strong> fetch catalog + packages when missing or outdated. No manual <code>.txz</code> steps.
      </blockquote>

      <dl>
        <dt>Install on array start:</dt>
        <dd>
          <select name="install_on_start">
            <?= mk_option($cfg['install_on_start'] ?? 'yes', 'yes', 'Yes (recommended)') ?>
            <?= mk_option($cfg['install_on_start'] ?? 'yes', 'no', 'No') ?>
          </select>
        </dd>
      </dl>
      <blockquote class="inline_help">
        Reinstall into the live (RAM) system after reboot — Unraid does not keep packages across boot.
      </blockquote>

      <dl>
        <dt>Catalog URL (advanced):</dt>
        <dd>
          <input type="text" name="package_base_url" style="width:min(32em,100%)"
            value="<?= htmlspecialchars($cfg['package_base_url'] ?? '') ?>"
            placeholder="default: GitHub packages/manifest.json">
        </dd>
      </dl>
      <blockquote class="inline_help">
        Leave empty for the official catalog. Only change if you host a mirror.
      </blockquote>
    </div>

    <div class="frr-section">
      <h3>Core daemons</h3>
      <p class="frr-section-lead">Leave Yes for typical fabric / OpenFabric use with Thunderbolt Net.</p>

      <dl>
        <dt>Enable zebra:</dt>
        <dd>
          <select name="enable_zebra">
            <?= mk_option($cfg['enable_zebra'] ?? 'yes', 'yes', 'Yes (required for routing)') ?>
            <?= mk_option($cfg['enable_zebra'] ?? 'yes', 'no', 'No') ?>
          </select>
        </dd>
      </dl>
      <blockquote class="inline_help">Kernel RIB/FIB. Leave Yes for almost all uses.</blockquote>

      <dl>
        <dt>Enable fabricd (OpenFabric):</dt>
        <dd>
          <select name="enable_fabricd">
            <?= mk_option($cfg['enable_fabricd'] ?? 'yes', 'yes', 'Yes (default — multi-hop fabric)') ?>
            <?= mk_option($cfg['enable_fabricd'] ?? 'yes', 'no', 'No') ?>
          </select>
        </dd>
      </dl>
      <blockquote class="inline_help">
        OpenFabric daemon for multi-host mesh/ring. Policy/metrics still configured on Thunderbolt Net when using TB.
      </blockquote>

      <dl>
        <dt>Enable staticd:</dt>
        <dd>
          <select name="enable_staticd">
            <?= mk_option($cfg['enable_staticd'] ?? 'yes', 'yes', 'Yes') ?>
            <?= mk_option($cfg['enable_staticd'] ?? 'yes', 'no', 'No') ?>
          </select>
        </dd>
      </dl>
      <blockquote class="inline_help">Static route helper in FRR. Safe default Yes.</blockquote>
    </div>

    <div class="frr-section">
      <h3>Optional protocols</h3>
      <p class="frr-section-lead">Default all No — enable only what you use (not needed for OpenFabric/TB alone).</p>
      <div class="frr-daemon-grid">
        <label>bgpd
          <select name="enable_bgpd"><?= mk_option($cfg['enable_bgpd'] ?? 'no', 'no', 'No') ?><?= mk_option($cfg['enable_bgpd'] ?? 'no', 'yes', 'Yes') ?></select>
        </label>
        <label>ospfd
          <select name="enable_ospfd"><?= mk_option($cfg['enable_ospfd'] ?? 'no', 'no', 'No') ?><?= mk_option($cfg['enable_ospfd'] ?? 'no', 'yes', 'Yes') ?></select>
        </label>
        <label>ospf6d
          <select name="enable_ospf6d"><?= mk_option($cfg['enable_ospf6d'] ?? 'no', 'no', 'No') ?><?= mk_option($cfg['enable_ospf6d'] ?? 'no', 'yes', 'Yes') ?></select>
        </label>
        <label>isisd
          <select name="enable_isisd"><?= mk_option($cfg['enable_isisd'] ?? 'no', 'no', 'No') ?><?= mk_option($cfg['enable_isisd'] ?? 'no', 'yes', 'Yes') ?></select>
        </label>
        <label>bfdd
          <select name="enable_bfdd"><?= mk_option($cfg['enable_bfdd'] ?? 'no', 'no', 'No') ?><?= mk_option($cfg['enable_bfdd'] ?? 'no', 'yes', 'Yes') ?></select>
        </label>
      </div>
      <blockquote class="inline_help">
        Advanced FRR protocols. Leave No unless you deliberately run BGP/OSPF/IS-IS/BFD on this host.
